   My objection to using ganlo(/kalri) for these cases (even in lujvo form)
is that the definition seems to be too narrowly defined
("portal/passage/entrance-way" access)  That would certainly be useful in
describing one trying to get INTO the school building, but not the fact
that physical access may be free, but the normal operation is suspended.
 That's why I suggested spofu as a more metaphoric sense of not available
for a normal function.
            --gejyspa


